# Test Code Boundaries

- Keep test-only helpers, fixtures, mocks, and setup in test folders or shared test setup files.
- Do not add production branches, production-only types, or production exports only to make a test pass.
- Use the production public contract. Do not reach into private implementation details when a user-visible result can prove the behavior.
- Keep fixtures named for the scenario they model. Do not use vague fixture names such as `data` or `result`.
